---
title: Pandionidae
---
# Pandionidae

Pandionidae is a family of one genus and one species, the [[osprey]], separated
from the other birds of prey by a reversible outer toe and dense, oily plumage.
Unlike most raptors it catches fish almost exclusively, and the spiny scales
under the foot are an adaptation to holding a wet, struggling fish in flight.
The family's isolation has been confirmed repeatedly by molecular work.
